# Production Improvements — Walkthrough

## Changes Made

### 1. Top-N Fallback Odds ([arb_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py))

Replaced [_get_best_odds_by_selection](file:///C:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#62-68) (single best) with [_get_top_n_odds_by_selection](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#33-60) (top 3 from distinct operators, sorted best-first). Arb detection still uses the best price, but fallback candidates are now available for the paper trade rechecker or future operator cycling.

### 2. Rejected Candidate Logging ([arb_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py))

Both [find_2way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#127-222) and [find_3way_arbs](file:///C:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#224-320) now track and log rejection reasons:

```
📉 2-WAY scan: 1 arbs found, 3 below min (0.5%), 0 above max (20.0%), 1 same-operator
```

This tells you how many arbs existed but fell below your threshold — useful for tuning `min_arb_percent`.

### 3. Risk Filter Breakdown ([risk_filters.py](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py))

[apply_all_filters](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py#157-193) now logs per-filter rejection counts:

```
Risk filters: 5/8 passed | rejected by: stale_odds=2, suspended=1
```

### 4. Stale Odds (No Change Needed)

Already implemented: 60s prematch / 10s live in [filter_stale_odds](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py#32-60).

### 5. Operator Diversity (Deferred)

Skipped per your guidance. Top-N change lays the groundwork.

